This appears to be a CBP ruling on a "mandrel" that acts as a blind plug, similar to a blind rivet, where the head stays and the shaft breaks off. Candidates are 8307 (flexible tubing), 7318 (screws, bolts, rivets), and 7318.19 (other threaded articles) or 7318.29 (other non-threaded articles).

I recall a ruling on "Monobolt" or "break-stem plugs" classified under 7318.29.00 as other non-threaded articles. The head is a plug and the shaft is discarded, so the shaft is threaded only for attachment to the tool. The installed head is unthreaded, so I chose 7318.29.0000 (other non-threaded articles). Rivets fall under 7318.23, but this is a plug, not a rivet. Other possibilities are 8466 (parts of tools) and 7326 (other articles of iron or steel). A sealing plug for a bore is, in my view, most likely classified in 7318.29.0000 as a blind plug fastener, though 7326.90.8688 is also plausible. I'll go with 7318.29.0000.

{"hts_code": "7318.29.0000", "reason": "The steel mandrel's head stays installed as a non-threaded, rivet-like fastener plug while the shaft breaks off and is discarded, so it falls under other non-threaded articles of heading 7318."}
